      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput is just Fmax. For a motor-control unit at >=1 MSPS, Fmax only needs to be ~1 MHz, which is trivially met even with wide datapaths. The binding constraint is max_abs_err <= 2^-10. Accuracy is set by n_iter (dominant), data_width, and the guards. I focus n_iter in 10..18 (10 is the classic minimum for ~2^-10 class accuracy, going higher buys accuracy_bits for the second objective at the cost of area). data_width 12..28 lets the optimizer find the minimum W that still meets the error bound while also exploring the accuracy_bits trade-off. angle_guard -2..2 and frac_guard 0..2 cover the small accuracy/area knobs. This is the primary family for the area-minimum corner."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.4,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
